# Responsiveness, a11y & smoothness rules (Phase H of the audit)

## Mobile-first storefront

- Type scale: hero/page titles use `text-4xl sm:text-5xl md:text-6xl` — never raw `text-6xl` on mobile (`RESP-09`).
- Long-text containers (product card title rows, checkout lines, cart heading) need `min-w-0` + `truncate`/`break-words`. `flex` rows containing a label and a price need `min-w-0` on the label and `shrink-0` on the price (`RESP-06`).
- Grids must not be ≥3 columns at <360 px viewport (`RESP-08`).
- Sticky bottom bars on mobile must include `pb-[max(env(safe-area-inset-bottom),...)]` and the page must include a bottom spacer / extra padding so content isn't covered (`RESP-02`).
- Inputs use `text-base md:text-sm` to prevent iOS zoom-on-focus (`RESP-07`). 16 px minimum on touch.

## Touch targets

- Primary interactive surfaces ≥ 44 × 44 px (`RESP-05`). `IconButton` → `h-11 w-11`, `ColorSwatch` → `min-w-11 min-h-11`, `Button size="sm"` (`h-9`) is allowed only in desktop-only chrome, not on cart/PDP/quantity controls.

## Focus

- Every interactive element rendered in the storefront chrome (`StickyHeader`, `SiteFooter`, announcement bar, drawers, cards, gallery thumbs, sidebar links, accordion `summary`) gets the shared `focus-ring` utility (`RESP-04`, `RESP-14`).
- Dialog surfaces (`Modal`, `Drawer`) must wire `useDialogFocusTrap`, set initial focus inside the dialog, restore focus on close, handle Escape, and expose `aria-modal="true"` + `aria-labelledby` pointing at a visible heading (`RESP-01`).
- Decorative icons get `aria-hidden="true"`.

## Semantics

- `<button>` for actions, `<a>` (or `<Link>`) for navigation. Never `<div onClick>`.
- Headings cascade in order. Dialog titles use `<h2>` (not `<h3>`) and back the `aria-labelledby` (`RESP-13`).
- Newsletter / contact forms must be wrapped in `<form onSubmit>` even when the handler is a placeholder (`RESP-10`).
- Footer group labels use heading elements, not styled `<p>` (`RESP-10`).

## Reduced motion

- Always respect `prefers-reduced-motion: reduce`. For GSAP code, see `.cursor/rules/20-performance-bundle.mdc` (combined viewport + reduced-motion gate). For CSS transitions ≥ 300 ms, ensure the `@media (prefers-reduced-motion: reduce)` block in `src/styles.css` covers them.

## Status / color

- Status (drop status pills, error/success messages) must not rely on color alone — include a text label or icon (`SEC` policy). Drop status pills already follow this; new badges must too.

## Smoothness

- Scroll listeners must be `{ passive: true }`.
- Avoid forced layout reads (`offsetTop`, `getBoundingClientRect`) inside scroll/resize handlers. Use `ResizeObserver` and cache.
- Animate `transform` / `opacity` only. Never animate `width`/`height`/`top`/`left`.
- Debounce text inputs that drive expensive recomputes (≥ 250 ms — shop search is the model at 350 ms).

## The Oath motion tiers

Reference `oathBreakpoints.ts`: mobile `<768px`, tablet `768–1279px` (static layout, no WebGL/GSAP pins), desktop cinematic `≥1280px`. Manifesto and tenets are hidden below `xl` in DOM.

## Toast / overlay placement

- `Toaster` must use a responsive position (e.g. `bottom-center` on small screens, `top-right` on large) and respect safe-area insets (`RESP-11`).

## Admin CMS responsiveness

- Admin is desktop-first (≥ 1024 px). Below that, it must remain usable: `AdminSidebar` becomes a `Drawer` and the `AdminWorkspace` rail stacks under the primary column (it docks beside it only at ≥ 1280 px). Dense tables become cards. Don't ship admin layouts that horizontally scroll the entire viewport.

## Copy hygiene

- Source files must be UTF-8. No mojibake (`ΓÇö` instead of `—`, etc.) — `RESP-12`.
